# Athlete data integrity

Completed sessions and logged sets are history.

- Change history only through an explicit edit or undo. Regeneration, import, and program updates must not silently rewrite it.
- Keep planned, performed, imported, and self-reported records distinct. Do not invent a date, set, load, hold, or PR.
- Store one canonical unit value. Repeating a pounds/kilograms conversion must not compound the number.
- A repeated save, retry, or double submit commits one set.
- A draft, preview, or note stays out of history until the user commits it.
- Deleting or migrating stored athlete records still requires the approval in `approval-before-destructive-operations.mdc`.
